<body>
    <h1>Meeting Minutes of 2026/07/20 - Q2 discussion</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p local-id=3D"fa9b7025fa60">Hi all,</p>
<p local-id=3D"b42a907d5534">&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"8e0f6d151534">Thank you so much for your attendance. Please =
kindly check the meeting minutes below for the meeting.</p>
<p local-id=3D"dcfee8a8854e">&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"8f5ad109fc21">Date: Monday, 20th July, 2026</p>
<p local-id=3D"9190c201b7af">Time: 17:30 HK time</p>
<p local-id=3D"1e0b8312f82f">Attendees:Tao Huang, Loura Guo, Jiajin Zhong, =
Daijiang Xie, Yixi Wang, Suijie Song, Guangyuan Mu, Huifang Liu, Jiaxing Da=
i</p>
<p local-id=3D"4bf2edd9e16a"><strong>Quick Recap</strong><br>
This meeting primarily focused on AI knowledge sharing and goal planning fo=
r Project Checkpoint 2. Zhong Jiajin shared the differences between LNWiki =
and LNWT, explaining how LNWiki analyzes documents, extracts entities, and =
uses graph expansion to answer questions. Wang Yixi presented system evalua=
tion results, noting that while the system returns relevant results, rankin=
g needs improvement. The team discussed next-phase priorities, including mu=
lti-data-source integration, PDF processing (especially images, tables, and=
 formulas), toolset expansion, and Confluence integration. Tao emphasized t=
he importance of creating Confluence documentation, suggesting that each mo=
dule lead record their progress and ideas, and recommended standardized for=
mats for tracking feature development and performance improvements. The mee=
ting concluded with next-week action items, including Confluence page setup=
, infrastructure building, and performance monitoring.</p>
<p local-id=3D"5e002aef4f29"><strong>Follow-up Actions</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"24938363-0042-4136-b811-8cfa789c932f">
<li local-id=3D"3f3697e4-ea68-4046-b3c4-f6cff5548907">
<p local-id=3D"06df2942ad73"><strong>Dai Jiaxing</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"bfebf906-3e54-41da-80a9-47dc3840a3e0">
<li local-id=3D"85ecffe7-13fc-49c9-b69e-4eba2d77d702">
<p local-id=3D"1e7465fce3e8">Research and experiment with solutions for han=
dling complex PDF content (images, tables, formulas), including OCR and mul=
ti-module understanding layer design.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ac25be6d-b6da-4679-9669-191c61559733">
<p local-id=3D"1ff2b319fdd1">Continue identifying and evaluating suitable E=
nglish datasets for future functional testing and performance assessment.</=
p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"fc2189fd-f93b-4619-a87a-d932e1cf8a03">
<p local-id=3D"0359ae05d517"><strong>Wang Yixi</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"527d06c3-c650-433c-a2aa-cb23284f7e34">
<li local-id=3D"ddbc5d6c-fb95-4c4a-b7bc-e9e26bd1a00e">
<p local-id=3D"aba6e2cee83d">Complete the Confluence page for data layer pr=
ocessing within the next week.</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"a163d18b-76d0-4428-9630-f7adab19e63e">
<p local-id=3D"546d09c7ccb2"><strong>Mu Guangyuan</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"2a66ee8e-c78f-4b26-83ff-f62c6bfaa729">
<li local-id=3D"a210830f-8b34-4e98-815b-f234ec0ade17">
<p local-id=3D"e7c7a3846958">Manage and maintain Confluence pages, organizi=
ng and documenting progress, feature ideas, and contributions for each modu=
le.</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"636f3072-94f5-41a2-b922-3706673c513a">
<p local-id=3D"3f605d0f8144"><strong>Dai Jiaxing</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"e3e104ac-2b26-44d7-af32-4ddc83288437">
<li local-id=3D"c59b4721-54c8-49c1-acac-80422f8684c0">
<p local-id=3D"b04a4ba27bc9">Responsible for taking and compiling these mee=
ting minutes.</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"fc621a83-ea67-4067-9b74-2f54b8e6ab13">
<p local-id=3D"97d1460b4580"><strong>Collaboration</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"d96f4b7d-5363-4e69-a71b-a0b9a0a32980">
<li local-id=3D"1ea3bdaa-bed5-42df-865d-07a9b1c02b5e">
<p local-id=3D"52d1bdfe4f97"><strong>All members:</strong>&nbsp;Create Conf=
luence pages for their respective modules by next Monday, summarizing imple=
mented features during the CPU phase, planned features for the CPR phase, a=
nd encountered issues, while documenting progress in writing.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"79b35399-9baf-4cb5-b856-187e7556fae3">
<p local-id=3D"ec76ed4dc97a"><strong>All members:</strong>&nbsp;When develo=
ping new features or optimizations, ensure clear interface definitions (inp=
ut/output specifications) are provided and recorded in Confluence.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"faf55da7-dbea-478a-be04-94dddcf078b1">
<p local-id=3D"1ec77a7dae1d"><strong>Web layer lead:</strong>&nbsp;Set up b=
asic system observability infrastructure, including query performance (e.g.=
, response time) monitoring.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b000176b-9df6-46c8-b8ac-b6c903b3a8cb">
<p local-id=3D"a43bd9fc1bae"><strong>Integration layer lead:</strong>&nbsp;=
Optimize the re-ranking algorithm, considering better ranking models.</p></=
li>
<li local-id=3D"08a4b6bb-4ad9-4047-b92e-9a1303d9c2fb">
<p local-id=3D"7a4d1ac1ec83"><strong>All members:</strong>&nbsp;Starting ne=
xt week, each team meeting should include 1=E2=80=933 slides summarizing la=
st week's accomplishments, challenges faced, and next week's goals, to be s=
hared during the session.</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"88320b249c2f"><strong>Summary</strong></p>
<p local-id=3D"d992e99d76e6"><strong>=E2=80=82=E2=80=82=E2=80=82=E2=80=82LL=
MWiki vs. RAG Technology Comparison</strong><br>
Zhong Jiajin shared AI knowledge on LLMWiki , distinguishing how these tech=
nologies process documents and answer questions. LLMWiki organizes knowledg=
e by analyzing key entities in documents and generating structured wiki pag=
es, while LLMWiki employs graph expansion techniques to discover inter=E2=
=80=91document connections and uses a four=E2=80=91signal model to assess r=
elevance. Zhong summarized the differences between LNWiki and traditional R=
AG systems in terms of processing approach, knowledge state, retrieval meth=
ods, and efficiency.</p>
<p local-id=3D"c5eacba3b309"><strong>Knowledge Graph Construction &amp; Doc=
ument Processing</strong><br>
=E2=80=82=E2=80=82=E2=80=82=E2=80=82The team discussed technical aspects of=
 knowledge graph construction and document handling. Zhong explained how LN=
Wiki parses documents to generate metadata, including entity extraction and=
 text structuring. Wang Yixi reported evaluation results, showing the syste=
m effectively retrieves relevant documents but requires ranking improvement=
s. Dai Jiaxing outlined next-phase priorities: multi=E2=80=91data=E2=80=91s=
ource support, integration with different platforms, PDF processing enhance=
ments (especially OCR and handling images/tables), and toolset expansion.</=
p>
<p local-id=3D"36dfcde51a9d"><strong>Financial Dataset Handling</strong><br=
>
=E2=80=82=E2=80=82=E2=80=82=E2=80=82Dai Jiaxing shared a financial dataset =
comprising multiple PDFs, some containing flowcharts that OCR could not eff=
ectively extract. Wang Yixi noted that due to budget constraints, an end=E2=
=80=91to=E2=80=91end model might be more suitable. Tao suggested temporaril=
y deprioritizing image processing in favor of text handling and recommended=
 integrating with Confluence first to read article contents.</p>
<p local-id=3D"83cba413939b"><strong>Platform Data Extraction &amp; Optimiz=
ation</strong><br>
=E2=80=82=E2=80=82=E2=80=82=E2=80=82Wang Yixi emphasized the importance of =
platform data extraction and encouraged team members to independently explo=
re optimization and enhancement directions for their modules. Tao proposed =
creating dedicated Confluence pages to track progress and record implemente=
d features, with Mu Guangyuan volunteering to manage these pages. The team =
agreed that future meetings should focus more on each member sharing functi=
onal updates and work demonstrations for their modules, rather than having =
Wang Yixi unilaterally set plans.</p>
<p local-id=3D"5ddbb0f248d3"><strong>Feature Development Progress</strong><=
br>
=E2=80=82=E2=80=82=E2=80=82=E2=80=82Tao and Wang Yixi discussed progress on=
 feature development. Tao suggested that each sub=E2=80=91team summarize cu=
rrently implemented features at their layer and propose new feasible additi=
ons, with a goal of completing open discussion and feature planning by next=
 week. Tao also proposed standardizing team meeting agendas, including proj=
ect updates, knowledge sharing, and progress reports from each group, recom=
mending each group prepare 1=E2=80=933 concise slides to facilitate present=
ations. Zhong Jiajin confirmed the target of conducting feature discussions=
 and planning by next Monday.</p>
<p local-id=3D"1c63e5e69371"><strong>Confluence Page Tracking System</stron=
g><br>
=E2=80=82=E2=80=82=E2=80=82=E2=80=82Tao proposed creating a shared Confluen=
ce page to track team progress and resolve issues. Mu Guangyuan and Dai Jia=
xing agreed, and the group discussed page organization, including module=E2=
=80=91based sections, status tracking, and contributor information. Wang Yi=
xi mentioned the need for usage guidelines and suggested using English rath=
er than Chinese for documentation. The discussion also touched on performan=
ce test dataset selection, with Wang noting that existing datasets include =
various test scenarios useful for evaluating system improvements.</p>
<p local-id=3D"cc4b83f83d1d"><strong>System Architecture &amp; Interface De=
sign</strong><br>
=E2=80=82=E2=80=82=E2=80=82=E2=80=82The team discussed system architecture =
interfaces and tool integration. Wang Yixi advised everyone to expose stand=
ardized interfaces when implementing new features and register tools in the=
 tool table, rather than using overly complex implementations. Tao stressed=
 the need to clearly define input/output requirements, similar to API contr=
act design. Wang Yixi also outlined next week's work plan, including buildi=
ng the memory module, finalizing Confluence page processing, infrastructure=
 setup, and tool integration optimization. Mu Guangyuan requested that meet=
ing minutes be placed on Confluence, and Zhong Jiajin confirmed that Mu wou=
ld first set up the roadmap configuration on Confluence.</p>
<p local-id=3D"01fa3d82582b"></p>
<p local-id=3D"c4907af598bf"></p>
<p local-id=3D"9b2cd2d62398">Hi <strong>Daijiang</strong>&nbsp;and <strong>=
Huijie</strong>,</p>
<p local-id=3D"ed3586efd2e4">&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"044eebac0596">Kindly remind you that <strong>Daijiang </stro=
ng>will be the <strong>host</strong>&nbsp;and <strong>Huijie </strong>will =
be the <strong>MoM Noter</strong>&nbsp;of next weekly meeting. Please read =
above Notes and get prepared.</p>
<p local-id=3D"4d753ddc69be">&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"c80b88e36a8d">Kind regards,</p>
<p local-id=3D"19042ea92558"></p>
<p local-id=3D"40a2806914f3"><strong>Jiaxing</strong></p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
